# Project conventions

## Folders

- Express API lives in **`server/`**. React app lives in **`client/`**.
- Do not create or refer to `backend/` or `frontend/` in this repo.
- Say "server" and "client" in docs, comments, scripts, and env names (`CLIENT_URL`).
- Env files: **`server/.env.local`** (secrets; copy from `server/.env.local.example`) and **`client/.env`** only (public `VITE_*`).

## API versioning

- All HTTP routes are under **`/api/v1/`**.
- Server prefix: `server/src/config/api.ts` (`API_PREFIX`).
- Client base: `client/src/lib/api.ts` (`API_BASE`). Call `/auth/login`, not `/api/auth/login`.
- Local: leave `client/.env` `VITE_API_URL` empty and keep the Vite `/api` proxy. Production (cross-origin): set `client/.env` `VITE_API_URL` to the API origin and `server/.env.local` `CLIENT_URL` to the SPA origin.
- Breaking changes get `/api/v2` while `/api/v1` stays. Do not add unversioned `/api/...` routes.

## Postman (git + cloud sync)

- **One** collection only — do not create parallel collections per step.
- Git file: **`docs/postman/FMS-API.postman_collection.json`**
- Cloud IDs / checklist: **`docs/postman/SYNC.md`** (UID `31395184-5914500b-3ae9-4fe4-9371-f1b01cc92ff0`)
- When adding or changing any `/api/v1` route, in the **same change**:
  1. Update the JSON (request, sample body, variables, short description, useful tests).
  2. If Postman MCP (`plugin-postman-postman`) is **ready**, push the same update to that cloud UID (`putCollection` / request APIs) and add a short **collection comment** describing the change.
  3. If MCP is not connected, still update the JSON and note cloud sync as follow-up.
- Auth is cookie-based (`fms_token`); do not invent a separate Bearer-only flow unless the API adds one.
- Keep `baseUrl` default as `http://localhost:4000/api/v1`.

## Manual test guides (MD + PDF)

- Each implementation step gets **`docs/manual-test-guides/step-XX-<name>.md`** and a matching **`step-XX-<name>.pdf`** in the same folder.
- When you **create or materially update** a step guide MD, **generate the PDF in the same change** (do not leave PDF as follow-up).
- Command (from repo root): `npx md-to-pdf docs/manual-test-guides/step-XX-<name>.md`
- Also update **`README.md`** manual-test links if the step is new, and **`docs/FMS-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`** step list when applicable.
- See **`docs/manual-test-guides/README.md`** for the full checklist.
